cff-version: 1.2.0

message: “If you use this software or its outputs, please cite both the software archive and the associated doctoral thesis.”

title: “dengue_ctmc_spark_turkiye: A CTMC spark-phase model of dengue threshold crossing in Türkiye under CMIP6 scenarios”

abstract: >-
Reproducible R workflow for a continuous-time Markov chain (CTMC)
spark-phase birth–death model estimating the probability that a
transmission chain initiated by an imported dengue infection reaches a
prespecified operational threshold before extinction across five sentinel
districts in Türkiye under CMIP6 SSP1-2.6, SSP2-4.5, and SSP5-8.5 scenarios
during 2025–2075. The repository includes climate bias correction,
importation-pressure construction, analytical finite-threshold calculations,
Monte Carlo propagation of extrinsic-incubation-period heterogeneity,
numerical verification, sensitivity analyses, and post-hoc regression
summaries. Threshold attainment is an operational marker of a substantial
early autochthonous transmission chain and does not represent endemic
establishment or long-term persistence.

